{
  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: While `BuggyCarousel` uses native `<button>` elements and applies basic `aria-label` and `alt` attributes, it is missing the foundational ARIA pattern architecture and dynamic state communication required for a carousel. Sighted users receive instant visual feedback upon slide changes, but assistive technology users receive no announcement of slide updates, cannot determine which indicator is currently active, and have no landmark context to identify or operate the widget.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**:\n- *Predicted*: Missing `role=\"region\"` and accessible name identifying the carousel widget. (*Confirmed* \u2014 container is an unadorned `div`).\n- *Predicted*: Missing live region or status announcement when slide changes occur. (*Confirmed* \u2014 no `aria-live`, `role=\"status\"`, or `aria-atomic` present).\n- *Predicted*: Missing programmatic state on slide indicators (`aria-current`). (*Confirmed* \u2014 active state is communicated solely via CSS class `.active`).\n- *Predicted*: Incomplete slide structure without APG grouping semantics (`role=\"group\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"`). (*Confirmed* \u2014 images render in an unassigned `div`).\n- *Predicted*: Hardcoded/non-descriptive alt text. (*Confirmed* \u2014 generic fallback `alt=\"Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}\"`).\n\n---\n\n### Perspective Alarm Levels\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|---|---|---|\n| Screen reader | **HIGH** | Missing live region, missing `aria-current` on active indicator, missing container landmark & roledescription |\n| Keyboard-only | **MEDIUM** | Standard `<button>` elements used; lacks `aria-controls` relationship and roving tabindex for indicator group |\n| Low vision | **MEDIUM** | Indicator active state depends on CSS `.active`; must verify contrast ratio \u2265 3:1 against inactive state |\n| Cognitive | **MEDIUM** | No context for total slide count (\"Slide X of Y\") in slide area; user must count indicator buttons |\n| Vestibular & motion | **LOW** | Manual carousel with no automated transitions or autoplaying movement |\n| Auditory access | **LOW** | No audio or video content |\n| Environmental contrast | **MEDIUM** | Active indicator styling must not rely on color alone |\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings (blocks access)\n\n*No Critical findings: Keyboard navigation reaches all controls without trapping focus, and native buttons are operable.*\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings (significantly degrades experience)\n\n1. **Silent slide updates due to missing live region**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:16-21`\n   - **User group impacted**: Screen reader users\n   - **Pattern / Criterion**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 Status Messages (Level AA), SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When a screen reader user activates Previous, Next, or an indicator button, focus remains on the clicked button. Because there is no `aria-live` region or status container, the browser emits no announcement to assistive technology. Sighted users see the slide update immediately, while screen reader users receive zero confirmation that the action succeeded or what content is currently visible.\n   - **Fix**: Add a live status region or place `aria-live=\"polite\"` and `aria-atomic=\"true\"` on the slide container, announcing the current slide index and total count upon transition (e.g., `\"Slide 2 of 5\"`).\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: carousel-missing-live-region\nfingerprint: a11yc01live88f2\nsource: BuggyCarousel.jsx:16-21\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.3 Status Messages / WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern\nsection_508_fpc_context: WCAG 2.0 Level AA equivalent\nseverity: MAJOR\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, keyboard=LOW, low_vision=LOW, cognitive=MEDIUM\nevidence: BuggyCarousel.jsx:16-21: <div className=\"carousel-images\"><img src={images[currentIndex]} alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} /></div>\nreproduction_steps: 1. Mount BuggyCarousel with image array. 2. Tab to 'Next image' button. 3. Press Enter/Space. 4. Observe screen reader speech log.\nexpected_behavior: Screen reader announces the new slide index or description (e.g. \"Slide 2 of 3\").\nactual_behavior: No announcement is made; focus stays on 'Next image' button in total silence.\ntrend: new\n```\n\n2. **Active slide indicator lacks programmatic state (`aria-current`)**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:36-37`\n   - **User group impacted**: Screen reader users\n   - **Pattern / Criterion**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A), WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: The active indicator button communicates its selected state solely through the CSS class `className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}`. In assistive technology, all indicator buttons announce identically (e.g., `\"Go to image 1, button\"`, `\"Go to image 2, button\"`). Non-sighted users cannot determine which slide is active or where they are in the sequence.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'true' : 'false'}` (or `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'step' : undefined}`) to each indicator button.\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: indicator-missing-aria-current\nfingerprint: a11yc02curr44d1\nsource: BuggyCarousel.jsx:36-37\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value\nsection_508_fpc_context: WCAG 2.0 SC 4.1.2\nseverity: MAJOR\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, keyboard=LOW, low_vision=MEDIUM, cognitive=MEDIUM\nevidence: BuggyCarousel.jsx:36-37: className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''} aria-label={`Go to image ${idx + 1}`}\nreproduction_steps: 1. Tab to indicator buttons. 2. Inspect accessibility tree computed properties on the active button.\nexpected_behavior: Active indicator button exposes aria-current=\"true\" or current state.\nactual_behavior: Active indicator button exposes no programmatic state; state is purely a CSS class.\ntrend: new\n```\n\n3. **Carousel container lacks landmark role and accessible name**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:15`\n   - **User group impacted**: Screen reader and keyboard users\n   - **Pattern / Criterion**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (Level A), SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: The carousel container is an unadorned `div` without `role=\"region\"` or a contextual accessible name. Screen reader users navigating by landmark regions cannot discover or jump to the carousel, nor do they hear what section of content the controls belong to.\n   - **Fix**: Replace `<div className=\"carousel\">` with `<section className=\"carousel\" aria-roledescription=\"carousel\" aria-label=\"Featured Images\">` (or `<div role=\"region\" aria-roledescription=\"carousel\" aria-label=\"...\">`).\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings (friction but workaround exists)\n\n- **Slide item lacks group semantics and contextual position metadata**:\n  `BuggyCarousel.jsx:16-21`: The slide is rendered as an unadorned `<div>`. Per the WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern, slide containers should have `role=\"group\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"`, and `aria-label={`Slide ${currentIndex + 1} of ${images.length}`}` so assistive technologies announce slide boundaries and positional context. (WCAG 1.3.1).\n- **Non-descriptive image alternative text template**:\n  `BuggyCarousel.jsx:18-20`: Hardcoded `alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`}` communicates only an index, not the graphic's actual content or purpose. Images should accept descriptive text from the data model (e.g., `images = [{ src, alt }]`). (WCAG 1.1.1).\n\n---\n\n### Enhancements (best practice not met)\n\n- **Missing `aria-controls` relationship**:\n  `BuggyCarousel.jsx:23, 27, 33`: Previous, Next, and indicator buttons do not reference the slide container via `aria-controls=\"carousel-image-panel\"`. Adding explicit programmatic linkage clarifies which DOM region these buttons manipulate.\n- **Indicator list semantics**:\n  `BuggyCarousel.jsx:31-42`: The indicators are grouped inside an unadorned `<div>`. Wrapping them in an ordered list `<ol>` or a `<nav aria-label=\"Carousel pagination\">` clarifies the sequence and total count of slides to screen reader users before they interact with individual buttons.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions)\n\n- **Missing total slide count announcement**: Screen reader users arriving at the carousel cannot know how many images exist without navigating through all indicator buttons.\n- **Empty state handling**: If `images` is empty (`[]`), `images[currentIndex]` is `undefined`, and the indicators map will not render, but Previous and Next buttons will still render and display broken state.\n- **Dynamic focus handling / roving tabindex for large sets**: If a carousel has 10+ images, each indicator button is an independent tab stop. For large image sets, the APG recommends a tablist or toolbar pattern with roving `tabindex` and arrow key navigation.\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n- **Screen reader user**: Experiences the carousel as disconnected buttons and an image with generic alt text. When activating \"Next image\", nothing is spoken, leaving the user guessing whether the slide changed. The active indicator cannot be identified because `aria-current` is missing.\n- **Keyboard-only user**: Can reach all controls using standard Tab and activate them with Enter/Space. However, tab order requires tabbing through every single indicator; arrow key navigation is not supported.\n- **Low vision user**: Relies on high contrast for the `.active` indicator. If `.active` is styled using color change alone without an underline, border, or shape change, it fails WCAG 1.4.1 (Use of Color). Target size of indicator buttons must also meet WCAG 2.5.8 (minimum 24\u00d724 CSS px).\n- **Cognitive accessibility**: Sighted users see which slide is selected and how many exist, but AT users have no \"X of Y\" reference within the slide viewport.\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\n\n**Verdict: REVISE**.\nThe component does not require a complete rewrite (`REJECT`) because it already utilizes native HTML `<button>` elements for all interactive controls and avoids invalid ARIA semantics or keyboard traps. However, it cannot be approved (`ACCEPT` or `ACCEPT-WITH-RESERVATIONS`) because it is missing the core programmatic feedback mechanisms of the WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern: dynamic state communication via live regions, `aria-current` on the active indicator, and landmark/region identification.\n\n**Required Remediation for Upgrade**:\n1. Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'true' : 'false'}` to the indicator buttons.\n2. Introduce an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region that announces slide changes (`\"Slide ${currentIndex + 1} of ${images.length}\"`).\n3. Add `role=\"region\"`, `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"`, and an `aria-label` to the outer container.\n\n---\n\n### Open Questions (unscored)\n\n1. *Component Data Contract*: Will the `images` prop be updated to support objects with specific alt text (e.g., `{ src: string, alt: string }`), or is this carousel intended exclusively for decorative/ambient imagery (which would warrant `alt=\"\"` and `aria-hidden=\"true\"`)?\n",
